{"id":"01a0657e-13b5-7744-86a9-b029b7186d19","chapterSlug":"rw4-22 E","paragraph":356,"wording":"[Paladin]","event":"named","holderSlug":"durene","holderQuote":"I hear Durene hit the ground. My protector, my mighty [Paladin] knocked out. Just like that."}
{"id":"01a0657e-13b5-7280-8a31-01c6e942def0","chapterSlug":"rw4-35 E","paragraph":18,"wording":"[Paladin]","event":"named","holderSlug":"durene","holderQuote":"He’s dangerous. This Hob has a battleaxe and he turns, the sharp blade dripping with blood, towards Durene. And he seems less affected by the light she emits. He lashes out with his axe and she raises her shield. I see Durene shouting again. Now her shield glows. The Goblins and Hob around Durene stumble back as a wall blocks them from swarming my beloved [Paladin]. Durene grits her teeth. I see her plant her feet in the mud, raise her shield and shove. Goblins go flying through the air and the Hob stumbles back."}
{"id":"01a0657e-13b5-77d9-9db9-e8e836cd8802","chapterSlug":"rw4-35 E","paragraph":202,"wording":"[Paladin]","event":"named","holderSlug":"durene","holderQuote":"Now the three closest towns and almost all of the villages accessible in a day’s journey are under my protection. Under the protection of eighty-some warriors and Wiskeria, a [General], but a low-level one. My champion is Durene, a Level 14 [Paladin]. I’m worried. But Wiskeria comes by with a proposal, and it’s such a good plan that we send out messengers that night to each town and village. We have a plan in case the Goblins come in force. I hope we never have to use it."}
{"id":"01a0657e-13b5-7b23-8c57-699146a659d6","chapterSlug":"rw5-09 E","paragraph":23,"wording":"[Paladin]","event":"named","holderSlug":"durene","holderQuote":"She’s half-Troll. And a [Paladin]."}
